===Etymology 1===
[[File:Briar_rose_(3212229202).jpg|thumb|A sweet '''briar''' ({{taxlink|Rosa rubiginosa|species}}). Mudgee, New South Wales.]]
From {{inh|en|enm|brere}}, from {{inh|en|ang|brēr}}, {{m|ang|brǣr|t=briar; bramble}}. Compare {{cog|is|brörr|t=briar}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# Any of many plants with thorny stems growing in dense clusters, such as many in the ''[[Rosa]], [[Rubus]]'', and ''[[Smilax]]'' genera.
# {{lb|en|figurative}} Anything sharp or unpleasant to the feelings.
#* {{RQ:Authorized Version|Ezekiel|2|6|passage=¶ And thou ſonne of man, be not afraid of them, neither be afraid of their wordes, though '''bryars''' and thornes be with thee, and thou doeſt dwell among ſcorpions: be not afraid of their words, nor be diſmayed at their lookes, though they be a rebellious houſe.}}
#* '''1785''', {{w|William Cowper}}, ''{{w|The Task (poem)|The Task}}''<sup>[https://books.google.co.in/books?id=HqtbAAAAQAAJ&pg=PA168&dq=The+thorns+and+briers+of+reproof.+(Cowper)&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0ahUKEwiSlr2ewLXkAhUOcCsKHWbMBSgQ6AEIKDAA#v=onepage&q=The%20thorns%20and%20briers%20of%20reproof.%20(Cowper)&f=false]</sup>:
#*: Rov'd far, and gather'd much : some harsh, 't is true, / Pick'd from the thorns and '''briers''' of reproof, / But wholesome, well-digested ;{{...}}

